  data: {
    scoringRules: {
      summary: 'In Chinese 51, only hands of five cards in one suit score, using A=11, K/Q/J=10 and numeral cards 2-10 at face value; declaring a perfect 51-point hand scores double and play continues until a player reaches or exceeds the agreed target (often 500 points). In Japanese 51, a five-card hand is valued by adding the points in the strongest suit and subtracting the points in the other suits, so totals can be positive or negative, and the highest final total after a Stop call wins the deal.',
      winCondition: 'Chinese 51: Be first to 500+ points by making hands of five cards in one suit (A=11, K/Q/J=10, numeric=face). Japanese 51: Have the highest-scoring hand; sum best suit then subtract other suits; call "Stop!" when satisfied.',
